    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**One file, one method:** `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.service`.\n\n- New format `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`: CITY3 = upper-cased first three letters of the city, LAST3 = first three of the last name, NNNN = a **per-city** 4-digit sequence (one more than the owners already in that city, counted by filtering `findAll()` on matching city).\n- Extracted a small private `first3(...)` helper so the two three-letter prefixes share one null-safe, low-complexity path instead of duplicating logic inside `service`.\n\n**Membership number rebuilt for free:** `OwnerMapper.membershipNumber` builds `<customerCode>-M<YY>` by concatenating `getCustomerCode()`, so it now emits the new city-prefixed form automatically \u2014 no edit needed there, which keeps the touched-file count at one.\n\n## Structural-impact notes\n\n`AssignOwnerCustomerCode` is a tiny class (the one method), so `WMC_other \u2248 0 \u2192 max(WMC_other,1)=1` and the surrounding-context multiplier stays minimal. I kept `service` simple and pushed the shared substring/uppercase logic into a separate cohesive helper rather than growing the method's complexity, and I avoided adding a repository query method (which would have touched more files) by filtering in place.\n\nThe acceptance test's format assertion (`[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) and the full suite both pass.",
